{
  "target": "god:OrderManager",
  "diagnosis": "The class exhibits a classic 'God Class' anti-pattern, evidenced by a high Number of Methods (NOM=25) and a critical Lack of Cohesion (LCOM4=4). The code explicitly groups methods into four distinct functional clusters: order management, pricing, audit logging, and notification. This results in high coupling (DCC=8) as the class references many external classes (Customer, Order, Product, ShippingCalculator, EmailNotifier, etc.) to support these unrelated responsibilities. The high Weighted Methods per Class (WMC=49) further indicates that the class is doing too much work, making it difficult to test and maintain.",
  "suggestions": [
    {
      "title": "Extract Pricing Logic into PricingService",
      "rationale_metric_link": [
        "LCOM4",
        "NOM",
        "WMC"
      ],
      "expected_effect": [
        {
          "metric": "LCOM4",
          "direction": "down"
        },
        {
          "metric": "NOM",
          "direction": "down"
        },
        {
          "metric": "WMC",
          "direction": "down"
        }
      ],
      "sketch": "Create a new class `PricingService` that encapsulates `_tax_rate`, `_discount_rules`, and the methods `set_discount`, `discount_for`, `bulk_discount`, `set_tax_rate`, `apply_tax`, `total_with_tax`, and `shipping_for`. `OrderManager` should hold an instance of `PricingService` and delegate pricing calculations to it. This removes ~7 methods and 2 attributes from `OrderManager`, significantly reducing its NOM and WMC while improving cohesion by isolating pricing concerns."
    },
    {
      "title": "Extract Audit Logging into AuditLogger",
      "rationale_metric_link": [
        "LCOM4",
        "NOM",
        "DCC"
      ],
      "expected_effect": [
        {
          "metric": "LCOM4",
          "direction": "down"
        },
        {
          "metric": "NOM",
          "direction": "down"
        },
        {
          "metric": "DCC",
          "direction": "down"
        }
      ],
      "sketch": "Create a new class `AuditLogger` that encapsulates `_log` and the methods `log_event`, `history`, `last_event`, `log_size`, and `clear_log`. `OrderManager` should hold an instance of `AuditLogger`. This reduces `OrderManager`'s NOM by 5 and removes the dependency on `AuditEntry` from `OrderManager`'s direct references (though `AuditLogger` will now reference it), potentially lowering DCC if `AuditEntry` was only used for logging. It also improves LCOM4 by separating the logging component."
    },
    {
      "title": "Extract Notification Logic into NotificationService",
      "rationale_metric_link": [
        "LCOM4",
