          "direction": "down"
        }
      ],
      "sketch": "Create a new class `NotificationService` that encapsulates `_smtp_host`, `_sent`, and the methods `configure_smtp`, `notify`, `sent_count`, `outbox`, and `reset_outbox`. `OrderManager` should hold an instance of `NotificationService`. This reduces `OrderManager`'s NOM by 5 and removes the dependency on `EmailNotifier` from `OrderManager`'s direct references, lowering DCC. It also improves LCOM4 by separating the notification component."
    }
  ],
  "risk_notes": "Refactoring a God Class into multiple services requires careful management of dependencies. `OrderManager` will now depend on `PricingService`, `AuditLogger`, and `NotificationService`, which may increase its DCC if these new classes are not already referenced. However, the overall system cohesion should improve. Testing will need to be updated to mock these new services. The `OrderManager`'s public API might need to be adjusted if it currently exposes methods that are now delegated to the new services, or it can maintain a facade pattern to keep the external interface stable."
}
